            <td data-label="Stage 2: the second filter">{row.second}</td>
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>

  <h2 id="tools-ai">Tools and AI for colour-blind professionals</h2>

  <div class="split-grid">
    <div class="split-card split-card--grow">
      <div class="split-card__label">What helps</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Browser developer tools can simulate colour blindness, so you can check your own designs.</li>
        <li>Contrast checkers test text and background pairs against accessibility guidelines.</li>
        <li>Phone apps name colours through the camera for everyday choices.</li>
        <li>AI assistants can describe a chart or suggest an accessible palette.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
    <div class="split-card split-card--risk">
      <div class="split-card__label">What to watch</div>
      <ul>
        <li>Apps can misjudge colour in poor light. Treat them as aids, not as final answers.</li>
        <li>AI descriptions of images can be wrong, so check anything that matters.</li>
        <li>Safety roles still need the formal test. No tool replaces it.</li>
        <li>Basic design work is being automated, so build judgment and client trust beyond palette choices.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </div>

  <p>
    Start now with a simulator and a contrast checker. Later, as tools mature, learn to audit AI output
    for accessibility and to build a repeatable review process. Pair domain knowledge with clear
    communication and proof others can see.
  </p>

  <h2 id="honesty">Never try to beat the test</h2>

  <p>
    Memorising Ishihara plates can feel like a shortcut. Review boards use other tests, and a hidden
    deficiency in a safety role can fail you later, at higher cost.
  </p>

  <p>
    Give an honest result and plan around it. A clear method for handling colour impresses employers
    more than a trick, and it keeps you out of legal trouble.
  </p>

  <h2 id="money">Money: protect it before the medical</h2>

  <p>
    Spend about a tenth of the family's education budget on the college fee, as a rule of thumb and
    not a research finding. If a route needs a coaching fee, a flying school deposit or an entrance
    fee, add those up and check the medical standard first.
  </p>

  <p>
    A colour vision deficiency on its own does not usually qualify for the disability scholarships. Check
    the scheme rules before you rely on them. Free and low-cost learning in software, data and design is
    available, but judge each course on the teacher's recent work and the feedback you get.
  </p>

  <p class="note-line">
    The rules and rulings above come from the sources named in the text, checked on 30 October 2026. We
    give no salary figures because we found no dependable source for these routes.
  </p>

